Third-party components
----------------------
Bundled components keep their own licences and are not covered by the terms
above:

  - Stockfish (https://stockfishchess.org/) - GPLv3. Distributed unmodified and
    launched as a separate process.
  - python-chess - GPL-3.0-or-later. Used in-process for PGN parsing, move
    generation, and puzzle validation. Redistributing a combined work may
    trigger the GPL's source-availability requirements; review before
    distribution.
  - openai - Apache-2.0. API client.
  - python-dotenv - BSD-3-Clause. Local .env loader.
  - numpy - BSD-3-Clause, with bundled 0BSD, MIT, Zlib, and CC0 components.
  - onnxruntime - MIT.
  - cryptography - Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause.
  - The Lichess puzzle database (https://database.lichess.org/) - CC0.
  - The Lichess piece sets listed in the README Credits - GPLv2+ / Apache-2.0 /
    MIT / CC BY / CC0, each owned by its author.
  - Qt / PySide6 - LGPL-3.0, linked dynamically.
  - PyInstaller - GPL-2.0-or-later with its bootloader exception; used to
    build the Windows and macOS packages.
  - Inno Setup - used to build the installer.
